-- ============================================================================
-- ALL DAY — round five: the Mind board for Body. One small paste.
--
-- Project:  jnouvwxomrcffqwilqkq (the fleet's one shared project)
-- Prefix:   nn_
-- Written:  2026-10-30
-- Needs:    nn-SETUP.sql, nn-ROUND2.sql, nn-ROUND3.sql, nn-ROUND4.sql and
--           nn-PLAYLISTS.sql, already pasted. It carries every board in
--           nn-APPS.sql too, so it is safe whether or not that was pasted.
--
-- How to run: Supabase dashboard -> SQL Editor -> New query -> paste this
-- WHOLE file -> Run. It should say "Success. No rows returned". Safe to run
-- again. Check it took:
--   select public.nn_rules() -> 'boards' -> 'mind';
--
-- What it does, in plain words: it replaces one function, nn_rules(), with
-- the same rules plus one new board, "mind", and one kind of post, "sit": a
-- short note about a sit, no photo, gone after 30 days. A reader who is
-- signed in can post one from Body's Mind tab. Every note waits for Stephen
-- on the boards desk (mod.html) before it shows, the way a gathering does and
-- the Lake Breath wall's notes did. After that it has the same reports, the
-- same two-reports-and-it-hides rule, and the same limits as every board.
-- Nothing else changes: no table, column, row, policy or grant is touched.
--
-- Until this is pasted the Mind tab hides the notes, the People button and
-- the Post button, and the sit and the headlines work on their own.
--
-- The rules stay at version 3 (nothing was taken away and no field type is
-- new). This is the same JSON as RULES in all-day/js/boards-core.js and as
-- the copies in nn-ROUND4.sql, nn-PLAYLISTS.sql and nn-APPS.sql;
-- scripts/test-boards-core.mjs fails if any two differ. Undo: paste nn-APPS.sql
-- from before 2026-10-30 (the board's posts stay in the table, unlisted).
-- ============================================================================

